1
00:05:08,181 --> 00:05:14,181
Lemonade Mouth is a drama, comedy, music film directed by Patricia Riggen.

2
00:10:16,363 --> 00:10:22,363
When five ragtag freshman first meet in detention, it
seems they have nothing in common.

3
00:15:24,545 --> 00:15:30,545
But, through music, they form an unbreakable bond and discover they have the
makings of the greatest high school garage band in history!

4
00:20:32,727 --> 00:20:38,727
In the face of incredible odds, Olivia, Stella, Wen, Mohini and Charlie find they can make a real difference
when they learn to lean on each other and let go of everything holding back their dreams.

5
00:25:40,909 --> 00:25:46,909
Olivia, played by Bridgit Mendler.

6
00:30:49,090 --> 00:30:55,090
Charlie, played by Blake Michael.

7
00:35:57,272 --> 00:36:03,272
Wen, played by Adam Hicks.

8
00:41:05,454 --> 00:41:11,454
Stella, played by Hayley Kiyoko.

9
00:46:13,636 --> 00:46:19,636
Mohini, played by Naomi Scott.

10
00:51:21,818 --> 00:51:27,818
Scott, played by Nick Roux.

11
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Lemonade Mouth is a 2011 American musical comedy drama television film produced by and
aired on Disney Channel as one of the network's original films (DCOM).

12
01:01:38,181 --> 01:01:44,181
Based on Mark Peter Hughes's 2007 novel of the same name, the film was
directed by Patricia Riggen and written by April Blair.

13
01:06:46,363 --> 01:06:52,363
It stars Bridgit Mendler, Adam Hicks, Naomi Scott, Hayley Kiyoko and Blake Michael as five high school students who meet in
detention and form a band to stand up for their values and to overcome their individual and collective struggles.

14
01:11:54,545 --> 01:12:00,545
Lemonade Mouth became the third most-watched DCOM premiere of its year with 5.7
million views, and DVR viewing raised the number to 7.1 million.

15
01:17:02,727 --> 01:17:08,727
The film earned a Popstar!

16
01:22:10,909 --> 01:22:16,909
Poptastic Award and nominations at the Directors
Guild of America and Golden Reel Awards.

17
01:27:19,090 --> 01:27:25,090
Its soundtrack reached number four on the Billboard 200 and produced the
Billboard Hot 100 singles "Somebody", "Determinate" and "Breakthrough".

18
01:32:27,272 --> 01:32:33,272
Lemonade Mouth received positive reviews from critics and audiences,
with praise for its direction, performances and themes.

19
01:37:35,454 --> 01:37:41,454
In the years following its release, it has been
considered one of the best DCOM films.

20
01:42:43,636 --> 01:42:49,636
The film explores themes of guitar, parent child
relationship, cat, violin, narration.

21
01:47:51,818 --> 01:47:57,818
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
